From 06681a933543984aef93fbe4f5085bb8f72c56df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Kohn <chris.kohn@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:13:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] README: document the boot header addresses in PRAM

The PLM reads the boot header, and on newer parts a hash block, from
fixed PMC RAM addresses that differ per part. Nothing recorded them, so
adding an architecture meant rediscovering them from embeddedsw.

Record the addresses per arch, where they come from, and that the header
in PRAM excludes the SMAP bus width table.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Christian Kohn <chris.kohn@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Mark Hatle <mark.hatle@amd.com>
---
 README.md | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 993b9a7..f5be037 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -7,6 +7,28 @@ the boot.bin, constructs appropriate qemu command line arguments and
 orchestrates the system level emulation for Zynq, ZynqMP and Versal
 families of FPGAs.
 
+## Boot header addresses in PRAM
+
+On Versal-family parts the ROM copies the boot header, and on the newer
+parts a hash block, into PMC RAM before the PLM runs. The PLM reads them
+from fixed addresses that differ per part, so a new architecture must use
+its own values or the PLM reads the wrong words and fails validating the
+image header table.
+
+The addresses are `XIH_BH_PRAM_ADDR` and `XIH_HASH_BLOCK_1_HASH_OFFSET` in
+embeddedsw, `lib/sw_services/xilpdi/src/<plat>/xilpdi_plat.h`. The hash
+block is loaded at its base, 0xa0 below the documented hash offset.
+
+| arch            | boot header | hash block |
+| --------------- | ----------- | ---------- |
+| `versal`        | 0xf201e000  | n/a        |
+| `versalnet`     | 0xf201e000  | n/a        |
+| `versal2ve2vm`  | 0xf201eec0  | 0xf201ecc0 |
+| `versal2vp`     | 0xf201ee00  | 0xf201ecc0 |
+
+The boot header written to PRAM excludes the 16-byte SMAP bus width
+table, matching `bootgen -dump <pdi> boot_files`.
+
